  "summary": "Forward 100\n\nThat was my first line of code in the third-grade, which made a little turtle move up 100 pixels on the screen. From that point on, I’ve been endlessly fascinated with the idea that a computer can follow my instructions to perform an action repeatedly. I’ve been coding ever since, most recently building tools that analyze large data sets and automate repetitive tasks so users can spend their time on things that they do best.\n\nSkills\n\nI truly enjoy working across the entire stack and seeing products through from ideation to completion -- wrestling with messy data sets to finalizing the behavior of a button. I’m most experienced with React.js, Flux, JavaScript, HTML, and CSS for the frontend and Python, Django, and postgreSQL for the backend. I consider myself a fast learner and am always happy to learn a new language (especially foreign ones!), framework, architecture, or library that helps with a project or end goal.\n\nGoals\n\nJust like my first line of code, I’m looking to move forward and to grow as a developer. I want to join a team that’s committed to developing its own talent through learning opportunities, collaboration, and mentorship. I hold myself and my work to high standards, and I want to work in an environment that fosters best practices and encourages quality code. Ideally I’d like to work in the languages and frameworks that I’m most familiar with, but I’m open to learning anything, especially if the tools and problems that I work on can have a profound impact on their users.",
